[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48115"] :question/problem "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=3?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $q(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have\n\n- $q(3)=0\\,$  exists  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}q(x)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}q(x)\\ne q(3)$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d7fc2426919c72ff934d19e98eb7465b8a42852407809d242213da9c26a4ed4a.png)\n\n   \n\nNotice that the functions $h(x)$ and $p(x)$ are continuous at $x=3,$ while $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=3$ but they are *not* removable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ca8fba5c-4423-5a82-823f-7e602b0e9309" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6c868039-c6bf-5e41-a903-d151527d60bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "75e55be7-ecaf-5ce3-9ace-15055cf1d531" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "12828aa8-0496-5f7b-b71e-512ec654adf7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "3634d29f-864c-5612-a3a0-2d1adfd25709" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b083d42b-d207-593c-9314-275453cff8f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47559/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-47559/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-47559/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-47559/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-47559/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-47559/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47559" :question/id #uuid "66cc33ab-f2ce-599f-8f13-d60a316244d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47559" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/613eaf413822013885a22df61a4bf32f7cd763bf11db71ab7b8769e19c0369b0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=0.$\n- It is continuous at $x=3.$\n- It has removable discontinuities at both $x=0$ and $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The function has a discontinuity at $x=0.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(0)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)\\ne f(0)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=0$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nIn the same way, the function has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(3)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=-2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)\\ne f(3)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I and III are true while II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff61d37b-595f-5dce-b4d5-fe70b3cf1d54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection/bcc3c118bafc1def339004d2280abf1a0dae67588aca23b3161baf681a4db77f" :answer/id #uuid "d5dfd831-51dd-5ac7-93bf-26ec100dc28e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/c6c9826ddd0cfc64cfa288b365c20c2e8bd67398f8f049a3ff80db13ab979d3f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection/f95c133b75751c114af5452c0837727d9b7e000f6508201dc15a8d8ec6bc81f9" :answer/id #uuid "3d5bbf9c-4a90-5cd4-bb16-dc91c6793378" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/340443e20bc285d2e711b81608a60eb81ff33537ece23860b11871f5373dfde2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection/fdb79417050da4cff4a6dd574f42473a307e8a9ee16e143100d691221c41eee1" :answer/id #uuid "bdd7f6f2-bd12-5f09-9020-2c0fa3970135" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/f1b1db6867e4629ba3155f5de1d59cdf36ed9190dbd7a18733bcbcf2f10402c5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection/3173b54841e13fda159a8d44e969380335a6693cc968efb3ecd60320f7b3b821" :answer/id #uuid "e032a4a5-0609-5f20-bed6-7913dde2af26" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/b77c43e9e33a958c65d6b3478b50c2f43e56d4a514bd092b50a9856d353a78f5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection/a146ba9280f572e5100d4c638c35180918df032ace3d4913c3481457b7305579" :answer/id #uuid "02859795-38ef-5fda-8de2-4bedcb02ceb5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/e82c2ab5ec147cbf2f6a6370aa10caaf23effdd672a2496add4bd72d2e5a9ab9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b281959e-3f6b-58ea-a79f-4478c4c7b384" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104387/selection/f95c133b75751c114af5452c0837727d9b7e000f6508201dc15a8d8ec6bc81f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-104387/selection/bcc3c118bafc1def339004d2280abf1a0dae67588aca23b3161baf681a4db77f" "q-104387/selection/f95c133b75751c114af5452c0837727d9b7e000f6508201dc15a8d8ec6bc81f9" "q-104387/selection/fdb79417050da4cff4a6dd574f42473a307e8a9ee16e143100d691221c41eee1" "q-104387/selection/3173b54841e13fda159a8d44e969380335a6693cc968efb3ecd60320f7b3b821" "q-104387/selection/a146ba9280f572e5100d4c638c35180918df032ace3d4913c3481457b7305579"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104387" :question/id #uuid "069bab20-c8c9-55e2-ad80-81ddc7c330e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104387" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=-3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)\\ne f(-1)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/340443e20bc285d2e711b81608a60eb81ff33537ece23860b11871f5373dfde2.png)\n\nNotice that the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are continuous at $x=-1,$ while $g(x)$ and $h(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=-1$ but they are *not* removable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104387/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff61d37b-595f-5dce-b4d5-fe70b3cf1d54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "87435c62-1d55-50c2-98cd-341e39a0afcd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4e308afc-b327-5302-9136-42a1190555f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "64db1116-b182-5719-b04e-614c938eb7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "e299d61e-d811-575f-8652-9c2781d8496e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5dae35eb-5ec0-53d0-af04-382decd66161" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da18e595-bfb7-5db8-b733-c988c6b371bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47516/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-47516/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-47516/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-47516/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-47516/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-47516/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47516" :question/id #uuid "3f6ba6a9-669c-53ec-9eb7-450cfe9629e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47516" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/4e796ff4d915d8c8b829574ade4eab05c7740de1f376d00900ec0d14b08f97d9.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- There are removable discontinuities at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is continuous at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nOn the other hand, the function has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(1)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)\\ne f(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true while I and III are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47516/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff61d37b-595f-5dce-b4d5-fe70b3cf1d54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47516"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48111/selection/9cd6e377f91ea19f25e2d3e399b40f847801376419210c2f6251cdc108c51cce" :answer/id #uuid "