n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo this time, the second condition failed, and therefore $x=-2$ is not a point removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=2$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "000408ba-6fbd-51da-9002-82fdde167a1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection/39f508abc01e725e09148a85c8f1573b302895828a712352740012f54d43f896" :answer/id #uuid "b2358219-bf2c-5892-89f4-753e3439b201" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection/fdb7062223b3ea91f42edb26b562ad404c5bbd4d148f8ce6a0c1ccb9b06634b3" :answer/id #uuid "5733a9d1-18ad-519e-9ec9-9a97247561af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=\\pm 3$ and $x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection/1ec5e6b6fa0e2a952c0543ef9b15eab2acd619bfc6363426322beee20fde07dd" :answer/id #uuid "d870378f-95df-54d3-a64c-6e38f02a29ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection/aabeb3321a25d4697e1a84b59fa42e07864928a32ea839539158940f0c6392e9" :answer/id #uuid "24b373c4-4db7-5b53-9c33-d3b529edd178" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer/id #uuid "62cfe893-faeb-5f5b-8512-a69e4e3743d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24f32f4f-d2ca-5fdc-8291-f4fdb87542c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48161/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-48161/selection/39f508abc01e725e09148a85c8f1573b302895828a712352740012f54d43f896" "q-48161/selection/fdb7062223b3ea91f42edb26b562ad404c5bbd4d148f8ce6a0c1ccb9b06634b3" "q-48161/selection/1ec5e6b6fa0e2a952c0543ef9b15eab2acd619bfc6363426322beee20fde07dd" "q-48161/selection/aabeb3321a25d4697e1a84b59fa42e07864928a32ea839539158940f0c6392e9" "q-48161/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48161" :question/id #uuid "a85b78fd-d65c-5ded-9498-c7b6781a7e0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48161" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/b92c2d0e713799d32f1be12b6cba56231af27ccc7a013e8726ab3b09289e69d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a point discontinuity?" :question/worked-solution "The function has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(3)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)\\ne f(3)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nNote that the function also has a discontinuity at $x=-3,$ but it is not a point discontinuity. Checking the conditions, we find that\n\n- $f(-3)$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo this time, the first condition failed, and therefore $x=-3$ is not a point discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=3$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "000408ba-6fbd-51da-9002-82fdde167a1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104415/selection/7838b39f8885d5d3061fc31f04257136e388eb217dbc966fb714a066b911ee9f" :answer/id #uuid "604ae4f7-9372-